      "writtenOn": "2022-02-08T13:24:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So the general approach for Zephyr for GPIO flags is to only include\nthe flags that define the physical pin config (voltage, pull-up/pull-down active-low etc.), and to define the extended flags like GPIO_INPUT and GPIO_OUTPUT in the gpio_pin_configure_dt() call.\nI do note that in your code where you do configure the GPIO, you set these flags,\nso I recommend you only use the flags that will fit into 8 bits, and use the standard macros like GPIO_DT_SPEC_GET.\nThe EC named-gpio bindings do allow setting of all the flags, but this isn\u0027t\nreally standard Zephyr.",
      "revId": "0f423dc5be6048830d429f6c1964182b57261285",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
